--------NLP PIPELINE--------
                Raw Text
                   │
                   ▼
        1. Text Collection
                   │
                   ▼
        2. Text Preprocessing
                   │
     ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
     │             │             │
 Tokenization  Lowercase   Remove Punctuation
     │             │             │
     └─────────────┼─────────────┘
                   │
                   ▼
          Stop-word Removal
                   │
                   ▼
     Stemming / Lemmatization
                   │
                   ▼
          POS Tagging / NER
                   │
                   ▼
       Feature Extraction
     (BoW / TF-IDF / Word2Vec /
        Keras Embedding)
                   │
                   ▼
     Machine Learning / Deep Learning
                   │
                   ▼
             NLP Applications
*review: this phone has a worst battery-> it is negative review
*it classifies the review

-------------RULE BASED NER---------------
->Rule-Based NER is a method of identifying named entities 
using predefined rules, patterns, and dictionaries instead of learning from data.
->entities are
*person
*location
*organization
*date
*time

----SPAM EMAIL IDENTIFING----
#this is for the rule based NLP to detect the spam
message=input("enter the message:").lower()

spam_words=["win","won","free","prize","offer","money","click"]
pro_words=["project","meeting","class","internship"]
is_spam=False
#for spam 
for word in spam_words:
    if word in message:
        is_spam=True
        break
if is_spam:
    print("spam email")
else:
    print("Not spam")

#spam word count
count=0

for word in spam_words:
    if word in message:
        count+=1
if count>=2:
    print("spam")
else:
    print("not spam")
#classifing using non spam keywords
if any(word in message for word in spam_words):
    print("spam email")
elif any(word in message for word in pro_words):
    print("not spam")
else:
    print("unknown")
#appied condition for is_pam and count
if is_spam and count>=2:
    print("spam email")
elif is_spam and count<2:
    print("not spam")
else:
    print("not known email")
